# MEMORY-RETENTION POSITIVE — NOT statically detectable. See README.md.
#
# The shape from
# doc/08_tracking/bug/native_build_worker_rss_unbounded_953mb_from_oom_kill_2026-08-23.md:
# a long-running accumulation that climbs to peak and releases nothing. Every
# line below is individually correct — the accumulator is mutated through its
# owner, there is no COW alias, no quadratic loop. The defect is that the
# retention has no bound and nothing ever drops entries.
#
# This is a LIFETIME property of a whole run, not a source shape: whether the
# growth is bounded depends on how many modules the caller feeds in and whether
# any consumer ever releases. A source lint sees only a `push` in a loop, which
# is also what every legitimate builder looks like. Detection belongs to a
# runtime RSS budget (peak reached 2.77 GiB, still climbing at ~40 MB/s, ~953 MB
# below the earlyoom kill), not to a static rule.
class ModuleAstCache:
    entries: [text]

    me record(module_source: text):
        self.entries.push(module_source)

    me build_all(sources: [text]):
        for s in sources:
            self.record(s)
